{
  "taxonomy_version": "1.2",
  "updated": "2026-10-12",
  "notes": [
    "Single source of truth for vocabulary categories. Never hard-code categories anywhere else.",
    "Two axes: 'hubs' (topic, with subtopics) and 'collections' (word type). A word has at most one primary subtopic, up to 2 secondary subtopics, and any number of collections.",
    "A word gets a full card only on the page of its primary subtopic (and that subtopic's hub). Secondary subtopics show it only as a small link, so pages don't duplicate each other.",
    "'keyword' is the proposed target query for the page. Each keyword belongs to exactly one page. Search demand is unverified: confirm with Search Console data before investing extra content.",
    "Each page's <title> is built from its keyword (e.g., 'Fruit Vocabulary with Pictures (60+ Words) | Muse English'); the visible H1 uses 'name'.",
    "'own_page': false means the subtopic is the core of its hub and never gets its own URL. It is always a section on the hub page, so the two can't compete for the same query.",
    "Words in the academic-words collection need confidence of at least academic_topic_min_confidence to appear on a topic page; below that they stay in the collection only (status unplaced). The Phase 0 review found abstract academic words were the ones most often forced into topics.",
    "'min_level' is the lowest CEFR level for planning lessons on this subtopic. A lower-level word can still be classified here (e.g., the A1 word 'food' in Diet & Nutrition).",
    "Slugs are permanent once a page is indexed. Renames need a 301 redirect and a taxonomy_version bump."
  ],
  "url_patterns": {
    "index": "/blog/vocabulary/",
    "hub": "/blog/vocabulary/{hub}/",
    "subtopic": "/blog/vocabulary/{hub}/{subtopic}/",
    "collection": "/blog/vocabulary/{collection}/"
  },
  "thresholds": {
    "page_indexable_min_unique_words": 40,
    "hub_preview_cards_when_subtopic_has_page": 12,
    "classification_min_confidence": 0.8,
    "academic_topic_min_confidence": 0.9,
    "max_secondary_topics": 2,
    "propose_new_subtopic_when_queue_cluster_reaches": 15
  },
